ng-boot-data-couchbase-test 4.1.1 maven artifact DataCouchbaseTest autoconfiguration"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01ScwU4p9eQDdkS6VCyJVjgA","tool_input":{"command":"find / -xdev -iname \"spring-boot-data-couchbase-test*4.1.1*jar*\" 2>/dev/null; find ~/.gradle/caches -iname \"*couchbase-test*\" 2>/dev/null | head -50; find ~/.m2 -iname \"*couchbase-test*\" 2>/dev/null | head -50","description":"Search local caches for the spring-boot-data-couchbase-test jar"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018k2TbBTWDzrmTkh6Wy8n6A","tool_input":{"command":"find ~/.gradle/caches -iname \"*couchbase-test*\" 2>/dev/null | head -50","description":"Search Gradle cache for couchbase-test artifacts"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_017EsS1v5rqZeCoZ7GNbKPJk","tool_input":{"command":"find ~/.m2 -iname \"*couchbase-test*\" 2>/dev/null | head -50","description":"Search Maven local repo for couchbase-test artifacts"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAHa4tyu9mftHYJBr5mzmR","tool_input":{"command":"env | grep -i gradle; echo \"---\"; find . -maxdepth 2 -iname \"*.gradle*\" -o -maxdepth 2 -iname \"gradle.properties\"","description":"Check for custom Gradle home env vars and root gradle config files"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzaMfLoqN6kbheJXE5JEeA","tool_input":{"command":"grep -rln \"testImplementation \\\"\\${\" forge --include=\"*.py\" 2>/dev/null; grep -rln \"def.*scaffold\\|new_library_scaffold\\|scaffold_new\" forge --include=\"*.py\" 2>/dev/null | head -20","description":"Find scaffold-related python scripts"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":42,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"## Decision\n\n**Research summary:** `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-data-couchbase-test:4.1.1` is part of Spring Boot 4.x's module split — it's the test-slice support module (holding `@DataCouchbaseTest` and its `TypeExcludeFilter`) for the sibling `spring-boot-data-couchbase` autoconfiguration module, which this repo just merged in #10423 (commit `0377c66108`). I found:\n\n- The merged `spring-boot-data-couchbase` test proved its autoconfiguration beans (`CouchbaseMappingContext`, `MappingCouchbaseConverter`, property binding, etc.) are fully testable via `ApplicationContextRunner` **without a live Couchbase server**, by deliberately excluding the core client autoconfiguration (`CouchbaseAutoConfiguration`, which lives in the separate `spring-boot-couchbase` module) from the tested slice.\n- No Docker image for Couchbase is pinned anywhere in `tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/`, and no test in this repo (including the existing `com.couchbase.client` leaf modules) connects to a live Couchbase instance — this repo has never needed one.\n- The Couchbase Java SDK's `Cluster.connect(...)` is non-blocking; it doesn't throw just because no server is reachable — failures only surface on an actual KV/N1QL operation. So even a slice-context-loading test exercising `@DataCouchbaseTest`'s imported auto-configurations is unlikely to need a live backend, as long as generated tests stick to context/metadata-level assertions (mirroring the sibling) rather than performing real repository CRUD.\n- Wiring to sibling modules (`spring-boot-couchbase`, `spring-boot-data-couchbase`, `spring-boot-autoconfigure`, `spring-boot-test`) as `testImplementation` is exactly what the sibling PR did directly in its generated `build.gradle` — ordinary, inferable groundwork the generation agent handles itself (build.gradle is editable post-scaffold), not a hard-to-infer per-library fact this preflight step exists to catch.\n\nNo concrete evidence surfaced for a required Docker image, extra dependency beyond ordinary sibling wiring, or a special environment/system property.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"no_action\",\n  \"summary\": \"Test-slice module (@DataCouchbaseTest) for the just-merged spring-boot-data-couchbase autoconfiguration; its beans are testable via ApplicationContextRunner/annotation metadata without a live Couchbase server, matching the sibling module's proven approach. No Couchbase Docker image is pinned in this repo and none is needed for meaningful coverage.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Favor ApplicationContextRunner/annotation-metadata style assertions over tests that perform real repository CRUD against Couchbase — e.g. verify @DataCouchbaseTest's imported auto-configurations, DataCouchbaseTypeExcludeFilter inclusion/exclusion behavior on sample @Document/@Repository fixtures, and annotation attribute defaults, the same way the merged spring-boot-data-couchbase test (tests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-data-couchbase/4.1.1) validated bean wiring without a live connection. Add testImplementation on org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-couchbase, spring-boot-data-couchbase, spring-boot-autoconfigure and spring-boot-test as needed, following that sibling's build.gradle.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"If local Gradle/Native-Image verification shows the slice annotation eagerly requires a live connection (contradicting the Couchbase SDK's documented non-blocking connect behavior), a CouchbaseContainer Docker image would need to be added — none is currently allow-listed in tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\nSpring Boot 4 split the old monolithic `spring-boot-autoconfigure` jar into dozens of small `spring-boot-<feature>` (autoconfig) and `spring-boot-<feature>-test` (test-slice) artifacts. The `-test` modules hold the `@XxxTest` annotations and their `TypeExcludeFilter`s — pure metadata/reflection classes — while the actual client wiring lives in the separately-versioned feature module they import. That's why checking the *sibling* artifact's already-merged test was more informative than trying to fetch the new jar directly.\n\nThe Couchbase Java SDK's non-blocking `Cluster.connect()` is the load-bearing fact here: unlike a JDBC `DataSource`, it won't fail context refresh just because nothing is listening on the other end, which is exactly what let the merged `spring-boot-data-couchbase` test exercise real autoconfiguration beans with zero Docker infrastructure.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────","ttft_ms":9839,"type":"result","duration_ms":329667,"uuid":"5cf2a20b-6caa-4b43-9470-93812d50ffb4","ttft_stream_ms":2270,"time_to_request_ms":114,"first_content_frame_ms":2270,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

